  <h1>What’s next for HELM</h1>
  <p>
    HELM is a simple framework with guides for working with AI agents. Our focus
    is to make it easier to understand and use, starting with product and
    engineering teams.
  </p>
  <h2 id="now-next-and-later">Now, next, and later</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Now:</strong> make the existing guidance clearer and easier to
      apply.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Next:</strong> a short way to discuss shared skills and choose
      what to practice.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Possible later addition:</strong> a short playbook for trying HELM
      on one piece of work.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="shared-competencies-and-development">
    Shared skills and development
  </h2>
  <p>
    Start with{' '}
    <a href="/competencies">
      five shared skills and role-based practice guides
    </a>
    : Judgment, Communication, Evaluation, Ownership and Learning. Choose a
    skill and your role for practical steps, an illustrative example and a small
    exercise to try in your next piece of work.
  </p>
  <p>The conversation will start with three questions:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>What does good work look like?</li>
    <li>What example from your work helps you reflect on it?</li>
    <li>What would you like to practice next?</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A more structured development review is still planned. We’ll try it with
    people in different roles and simplify anything confusing before sharing
    that method. The current examples support learning and feedback.
  </p>
  <h2 id="work-redesign-kit-and-pilot">
    A short playbook to try with your team
  </h2>
  <p>
    If readers need more help getting started, we may add a short playbook:
    choose one piece of work, agree what the agent can do and who checks it,
    then discuss what to keep or change. We’ll try it with a team first and keep
    it only if it helps.
  </p>
